redfin 1093: router answers for CommCenter's Apple AUDIO (0xe1) vocoder messages (coder V, 2026-11-14). BBA study A2.
- kern.sweet_qmi_vocoder 0 (default: the policy's blank "ok", unchanged) / 1: 0x002f GetVocoderType -> TLV 0x01
  {type, rate kHz}; 0x0030 VocoderTypeInfo indication (TLV 0x01 + 0x10 I2S clock kHz) to CommCenter's 0xe1 client at a
  call's voice start and when the modem's speech codec changes. I2S = the proxy's rate (16 kHz without a proxy);
  vocoder rate = the modem's codec (VOICE ind kern.sweet_qmi_codec_ind, TLV kern.sweet_qmi_codec_tlv 0x11, qcril
  CODEC_* numbering) else the I2S rate; the log names the source. kern.sweet_qmi_codec_ind 0 = learn (VOICE indication
  ids logged once, TLV ids/lengths only). kern.sweet_qmi_vocoder_type (default 0x10). sweet_voice.c notes call start/end.

